  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Infernal Pact",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2097448-infernal-pact"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat, introduced in “D&D Beyond Drops”, gives you incredible fiendish power with all of the Warlock flavor and none of the class levels. Damage resistances and Devil’s Sight are both amazing on literally any character."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Infernal Pact is excellent if someone in your party is building to rely on magical darkness. Normally, you need an option like Fighting Style (Blind Fighting) or the Devil’s Sight invocation to see through magical darkness. Infernal Pact solves that challenge without multiclassing, allowing entire parties to easily build around fighting inside a Darkness spell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "From a balance perspective, this feat is crazy. A Ring of Resistance is a Rare magic item, and this gives you the benefits of two. That’s great on its own, then you add Devil’s Sight on top of it and a skill proficiency because apparently they wanted a third bullet point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Infernal Pact is required for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Infernal Bulwark",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/infernal-bulwark/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Infernal Dragoon",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/infernal-dragoon/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Infernal Pact received errata in the August 2026 Drops, reducing Infernal Resistance to one resistance and reducing the range on Infernal Sight to 30 feet. This was a much-needed nerf to an exceptionally powerful feat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-infernal-resistance",
      "heading": "Infernal Resistance",
      "sourceAnchor": "infernal-resistance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-infernal-resistance-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Resistance your choice of the two most common non-weapon damage types in the game. Absolutely fantastic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-infernal-sight",
      "heading": "Infernal Sight",
      "sourceAnchor": "infernal-sight",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-infernal-sight-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Devil’s Sight within 30 feet. Amazing. It’s not as good as the Warlock’s Devil’s Sight Invocation, but it’s great for non-Warlocks in a party with allies that like to use magical darkness."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-silvertongued",
      "heading": "Silver-Tongued",
      "sourceAnchor": "silvertongued",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-silvertongued-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "One skill proficiency. Always great."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-5",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
